Added the `client_ip_headers` setting to the Audit log tab of the Identity providers control panel, naming the request headers that carry a visitor's real address, in order. It covers sites behind Cloudflare (`CF-Connecting-IPv6`, then `CF-Connecting-IP`) and behind a proxy that appends to `X-Forwarded-For`, such as on Docker Swarm, where the audit log otherwise records a container network address. The magic-link rate limit uses the same address. @ericof
